<title>SPAIN: Spain September C/A surplus 79.30 bln pta Bos. [CORRECTED 14:20 GMT]</title>
<headline>Spain September C/A surplus 79.30 bln pta Bos. [CORRECTED 14:20 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects the second column to August 1996 data. The original story incorrectly gave July 1996 data in the second column).</p>
<p>The Bank of Spain gave the following figures (in billions of pesetas):</p>
<p> BALANCE OF PAYMENTS		SEPT 96	AUG 96</p>
<p>  C/A balance			 79.30	   173.8</p>
<p>  Trade balance		   -236.40	  -133.5</p>
<p>  Services			   252.30	   328.6</p>
<p>  Net tourism receipts	   282.00	   339.3</p>
<p>  Other services		   -29.70	   -10.7</p>
<p>  Dividend income		  -66.60	   -10.1</p>
<p>  Transfers			  130.00	   -11.2</p>
<p>  CAPITAL ACCOUNT		   33.30	    36.6</p>
<p>  FINANCIAL ACCOUNT		-71.90	  -177.7</p>
<p>  Spanish investment abroad     93.90	   -96.2</p>
<p>  Foreign investment Spain   1,234.30	-1,168.3</p>
<p>  Spanish loans,dep abroad  -1,078.30	   642.4</p>
<p>  Foreign loans, deps in Spain-151.00	   490.8</p>
<p>  Movement of reserves	  -170.70	   -46.4</p>
<p>NOTE: The Bank of Spain said latest figures were provisional. Non-classified element (errors and omissions) in latest capital account figures is negative for 40.8 billion pesetas. The financial account category was introduced in January 1996.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
